    in which case they are stacked before continuing the computation.

    >>> x = jnp.array([-1, 0, 1])
    >>> y = jnp.array([1, 0, -1])
    >>> jnp.cov(x, y)
    Array([[ 1., -1.],
           [-1.,  1.]], dtype=float32)

